// LINTRAN - standard matrix of a linear transformation from input/output vectors.
// Columns of [A] = v1..vk, columns of [B] = T(v1)..T(vk). Finds T with T*A = B
// by solving A^T T^T = B^T.
// Out: [C] = standard matrix (free variables = 0 if it is not unique)
ClrHome
Disp "STANDARD MATRIX","T(COLS OF [A])","= COLS OF [B]"
dim([A])→ʟZD
ʟZD(1)→G
dim([B])→ʟZD
ʟZD(1)→U
augment([A]ᵀ,[B]ᵀ)→[J]
0→S
0→Q
G→W
prgmZRREF
0→O
For(I,R+1,M)
For(J,G+1,N)
If [J](I,J)≠0
1→O
End
End
If O:Then
Disp "NO SUCH LINEAR T","(INPUTS DEPENDENT BUT","OUTPUTS INCONSISTENT)"
Return
End
{G,U}→dim([H])
Fill(0,[H])
For(I,1,R)
For(J,1,U)
[J](I,G+J)→[H](ʟPIV(I),J)
End
End
[H]ᵀ→[C]
If R<G
Disp "NOT UNIQUE (INPUTS","DO NOT SPAN), ONE IS:"
Disp "STANDARD MATRIX [C]"
Pause [C]►Frac
